# .env.example — copy to `.env` and fill in what you need.
# `.env` is gitignored (.gitignore:22). Never commit real keys.
#
# Phase 0 status: no code reads these yet — every jarvis/*/__init__.py is empty.
# The entries below are the services the docs actually commit to, with the
# file that names each one. Add more as subsystems land; delete what you drop.
#
# Every line is commented out on purpose. This project is subscription-first:
# the Proposer runs on your ChatGPT subscription and the Critic on your Claude
# subscription, so the correct default for all of these is UNSET.

# ── Claude critic — docs/RULES.md rule 9, docs/MAC_APP.md:34 ───────────────
# LEAVE UNSET for normal operation. CriticAgent invokes the official `claude`
# binary against your subscription.
#
# NEVER put a Claude OAuth token here. RULES.md rule 9 forbids reusing it in
# any non-official client, SDK, or third-party tool — that is an account ban
# risk, not a style preference.
#
# Set this ONLY when flipping CriticAgent to its metered fallback path, which
# the docs require you to pair with `--max-budget-usd`.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ── OpenAI — embeddings / moderation only ─────────────────────────────────
# NOT used by the Codex collab bridge, and not used by the runtime Proposer.
# .claude/bin/codex-bridge.sh unsets this before exec'ing codex, so Codex
# always authenticates via ~/.codex/auth.json (ChatGPT subscription) and can
# never bill this key. Verified: the bridge's child process receives it unset
# even when it is exported in the parent shell.
#
# If you ever add a runtime path that shells out to codex WITHOUT going
# through that bridge, it will NOT get this protection.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# ── Verifier Gate fetch fallbacks — docs/ARCHITECTURE.md:73 ───────────────
# The citation pipeline falls back to these when a direct HTTP fetch returns
# 403 or needs JS rendering. Both are optional; r.jina.ai has a keyless free
# tier, so start without keys and add them only if you hit rate limits.
# JINA_API_KEY=
# FIRECRAWL_API_KEY=

# Wayback availability + Save-Page-Now need no credentials for the basic
# endpoints the Verifier uses. Add SPN S3 keys here only if you hit its
# authenticated rate limits.
